  "preview_bpm": 100,
  "editorial": [
    "On the first pass, take the two-bar segno lead repeat, then verse one. Sing the chorus pickup, play the common chorus, take First and return to the common chorus. First already contains the harmonized repeat pickup.",
    "Second leads back to the sign on page 2. This reading takes the two-bar lead once after D.S., then plays verse two and the chorus through Last. The barline repeats are used on the outward pass.",
    "First has a natural E in the piano cadence. Second flattens that E and leaves the voice at rest over the piano's C and E-flat lead-in to the D.S. The vocal guide follows the lower printed line at the optional ad lib.",
    "Both piano staves play throughout with independent lines for split stems. Tempo and velocities are fixed for rehearsal. Printed rolls sound together and fermatas retain their nominal values. Lyrics and scan images stay with the source."
  ],
